  "label": "Justin Trudeau is mapped as the source of the claim about Syrian migrants",
  "description": "The top text overlay 'we can not security check syrian migrants properly, but we can trust them.' is spatially positioned above Justin Trudeau's image, directly associating him with the claim. This creates an analogical mapping where Justin Trudeau (the visual entity) is implicitly mapped as the entity making or endorsing the claim about Syrian migrants (the textual entity). The meme uses his image to project the stereotype and policy position onto him, implying his endorsement or representation of the anti-Syrian sentiment.",
